From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:57:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claude: a fresh sign-in waits for runs in the account's
 directory (#6602)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#3254's fix guards ForgetLogin's removal of a saved account's
directory, but a fresh sign-in still removes it with no look at the
run marks (#4532): signing in again to a saved Claude account
replaces the older saved directory (addLogin, signin.go), and another
magpie process's run in it (a /usage, a warm-up, a keep-alive) had it
taken from under it.

addLogin (claude) now takes the account's in-process run mutex and
waits on every other process's run mark up to claudeRunWait, refusing
with errClaudeRunning past it, before loginsMu: the guard comes first,
the order every claudeDirRun holder keeps, and the sign-in flow
answers the refusal as a sign-in that didn't finish and asks to be
tried again. Nothing is written or removed under a run.

What changed:
- internal/provider/signin.go: the guard at the top of addLogin
- internal/provider/claude_lock_test.go:
  TestClaudeFreshSignInRefusedWhileAnotherMagpieRunsTheFolder
  (held/ended), the shape of TestClaudeForgetRefusedWhileAnotherMagpieRunsTheFolder

Run (darwin/arm64, go1.26.8, GOCACHE pinned, temp HOME):
- red before the fix: go test ./internal/provider -run
  TestClaudeFreshSignInRefusedWhileAnotherMagpieRunsTheFolder →
  held "got <nil>", ended "a left lock file kept: <nil>"
- green after: same command → ok (1.146s)
- ablation (guard reverted, test kept): FAIL as above; restored: ok
- go test ./internal/provider -run 'TestClaude|TestSavedClaudeRun'
  -count=1 → ok (21.696s)
- go test -tags nogui -timeout 25m ./... → ok in the touched package
  but TestResolveVia (provider; reproduced on clean base 80a315a70,
  the machine's proxy), TestMothX (agent; same on base),
  TestFreedHeapLeavesFootprint (build/darwin; same on base), four cli
  tests (same on base), TestProxyCheckSaysAProxyPassedBy (gui; same
  on base), TestHostToldTheGatewayAddress (plugin; same on base);
  TestSessionReadsRoutes and usage's 25m timeout pass alone on base
  and here (loaded-run flakes)
- go test -race ./internal/provider -timeout 25m → the two DATA RACE
  warnings (TestPluginCheckinAsksAgainAtUntil,
  TestSignInDoneOnceTheAccountIsBack, both in test files' globals)
  reproduce on clean base with -race
- gofmt -l on the two files: prints nothing
- go vet ./..., GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./...,
  GOOS=windows go vet ./...: clean
- go build ./..., GOOS=linux go build -tags nogui ./...,
  GOOS=darwin go build ./..., GOOS=windows go build ./...: ok

